From e68aecc3c36e3614a734efc1c23803ff8f68f2d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:34:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.9.9a: Wireless Diagnostics - Unlock confirmation +
 survive scanning your own band

Two field-driven follow-ons to v1.9.9:

- Unlock confirmation (RWIF_61): Unlock (like Lock and Pin) goes through
  restart_wireless, which fully restarts the radio and drops every client on it
  for ~20s - which reads as "the board froze". Per-frequency restart is not
  reachable (closed driver), so unlock() now warns before proceeding. New key
  RWIF_61 across all 25 dicts (machine-translated non-EN - review pending).

- Auto Scan of your own band no longer self-aborts after one channel: each scan
  candidate does a restart_wireless; if the admin's browser is on the scanned
  band it drops ~20s per candidate, and the 12s heartbeat then aborted the sweep
  (field: 2.4 GHz scan returned a single channel; user disconnected ~2s in).
  RWIFI_SCAN_HB 12 -> 60s so the sweep survives each per-candidate reconnect gap.
  The sweep is bounded (max ~12 candidates) and self-restores, so the longer wait
  for a genuinely-closed tab is harmless. Cleanest run is still from a wired
  client or a different band (the RWIF_33/RWIF_60 warnings say so).

Note: if a 2.4 GHz scan still returns one channel when run from ANOTHER band /
wired (no disconnect), that points to a candidate-generation format mismatch
(the parser expects bare 1/6/11 from `wl chanspecs`) - a separate, targeted fix.

Metal-only validatable (mock cannot render this page).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
